<div class="wp-block-group shead"><!-- wp:group -->
<div class="wp-block-group"><!-- wp:html -->
<span class="lab kick" data-r="">Technology</span>
<!-- /wp:html -->
<!-- wp:heading {"className":"d2 split"} -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading d2 split">Innovation in <em>specialty glass.</em></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading --></div>
<!-- /wp:group -->
<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Proprietary phosphate, germanate and tellurite glasses are the key enabler of our fiber lasers, amplifiers and ASE sources, and they open parts of the spectrum where silica is opaque: our tellurite fibers carry mid-infrared light from 2 to 5 µm.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>
<!-- /wp:group -->
<!-- wp:group {"className":"tri"} -->
<div class="wp-block-group tri"><!-- wp:group {"className":"cap"} -->
<div class="wp-block-group cap"><!-- wp:html -->
<span class="lab" data-r="">Phosphate</span>
<!-- /wp:html -->
<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">High gain per unit length</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->
<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Highly doped phosphate fibers give large gain in a short length, enabling high-power single-frequency lasers and short, low-latency amplifiers.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>
<!-- /wp:group -->
<!-- wp:group {"className":"cap"} -->
<div class="wp-block-group cap"><!-- wp:html -->
<span class="lab" data-r="">Germanate</span>
<!-- /wp:html -->
<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Efficient 2 µm lasers</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->
<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Low-OH holmium-doped germanate fiber gave 15.6 W at 2050 nm from a 10 cm fiber laser, at a record 80% optical-to-optical efficiency.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>
<!-- /wp:group -->
<!-- wp:group {"className":"cap"} -->
<div class="wp-block-group cap"><!-- wp:html -->
<span class="lab" data-r="">Tellurite</span>
<!-- /wp:html -->
<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Mid-IR transport</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->
<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Low-loss (&lt;0.2 dB/m) fibers with substantially no hydroxyl, to carry and distribute high-power mid-IR light from parametric, quantum cascade and supercontinuum sources.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>
<!-- /wp:group --></div>
<!-- /wp:group --></div>
<!-- /wp:group --></section>
